Subject: [PATCH] config: read /etc/daynight.state sidecar (raw open/read) as day/night source of truth
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (stacks on 0001-0014)

The two MQTT-frequent modes (auto/day/night) persist in a tiny atomic sidecar
/etc/daynight.state ("mode=auto|day|night") instead of rewriting the whole
~8.5 KB prudynt.json. CFG::load() reads that sidecar at config-load and sets
daynight.enabled + daynight.force_mode_cfg from it (after the prudynt.json item
loops, so it overrides them). IMPSystem::init() (patch 0001) derives the ISP
running_mode from force_mode_cfg before the pipeline is built, so a forced mode
sticks; S56ircut reads the same sidecar for the IR-cut/IR-LED optics. A missing/
unreadable/unrecognized sidecar => auto (safe default). One-time migration from
the legacy prudynt.json keys is done in the rootfs before launch.

CRASH FIX: the sidecar is read with RAW POSIX open()/read() -- NOT fopen and NOT
std::ifstream. On this Sonoff PT2 (T23 / uClibc-ng) prudynt is force-linked
against libuclibcshim.so (a glibc->uClibc ABI shim) which interposes fopen/fopen64;
reading the sidecar through libc stdio (std::ifstream's filebuf, or a direct
fopen) segfaulted inside that shim at prudynt startup, before the stream came up.
Raw open()/read()/close() bypass the shim and are the same primitives
DayNightWorker/ImagingControl already use successfully in this binary. The two
config members are set unconditionally (no strcmp of the prior force_mode_cfg,
so no deref of a pointer this code does not own; a 1-6 byte per-reload leak is
negligible).

Single file (Config.cpp): adds <fcntl.h>/<unistd.h> + the CFG::load read block.
Verified: git apply --check AND patch -p1 --dry-run both pass against
f4b3228 + 0001-0014.

diff --git a/src/Config.cpp b/src/Config.cpp
index 5861a39..06345d5 100644
--- a/src/Config.cpp
+++ b/src/Config.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdint>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include <filesystem>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <functional>
@@ -1400,6 +1402,64 @@ void CFG::load() {
     }
   }
 
+  // 0015: /etc/daynight.state is the single source of truth for the two
+  // MQTT-frequent day/night keys (daynight.enabled + daynight.force_mode). It is
+  // a tiny sidecar written atomically by the rootfs helper `daynight-state`, so
+  // toggling auto/day/night no longer rewrites the whole ~8.5KB prudynt.json.
+  // Apply it AFTER the prudynt.json item loops (so it overrides them) and
+  // UNCONDITIONALLY -- even when jsonConfig is null because the main config was
+  // corrupt/truncated and 0012 fell back to defaults. The sidecar is a SEPARATE
+  // file that survives a prudynt.json truncation, so honoring it here is exactly
+  // the power-outage recovery we want. Format: one line "mode=auto|day|night";
+  // a missing / unreadable / unrecognized sidecar => auto (safe default). prudynt
+  // never consults the legacy prudynt.json keys once a migration has created the
+  // sidecar (S31prudynt runs `daynight-state migrate` before launch). Because
+  // IMPSystem::init() derives running_mode (color/mono) from force_mode_cfg
+  // BEFORE the pipeline is built (patch 0001), setting it here is what makes the
+  // persisted mode stick on this sensor -- there is no late boot-script re-apply.
+  {
+    // Read the sidecar with RAW POSIX open()/read() -- NOT fopen and NOT
+    // std::ifstream. Both libc-stdio forms (filebuf->fopen, and direct fopen)
+    // segfault inside the T23 uClibc compat shim (libuclibcshim interposes
+    // fopen); raw open/read bypasses the shim and is the same primitive
+    // DayNightWorker/ImagingControl already use successfully on this build.
+    char scbuf[64];
+    ssize_t scn = -1;
+    int scfd = ::open("/etc/daynight.state", O_RDONLY);
+    if (scfd >= 0) {
+      scn = ::read(scfd, scbuf, sizeof(scbuf) - 1);
+      ::close(scfd);
+    }
+    scbuf[(scn > 0) ? (size_t)scn : 0] = '\0';
+    // Parse "mode=auto|day|night" from the buffer, skipping a leading quote/
+    // whitespace -- identical tolerance to the rootfs helper so prudynt and the
+    // shell can never disagree on a value.
+    std::string scMode;
+    if (const char *mp = std::strstr(scbuf, "mode=")) {
+      mp += 5;
+      while (*mp == '"' || *mp == ' ' || *mp == '\t' || *mp == '\r' ||
+             *mp == '\n' || *mp == '\f' || *mp == '\v')
+        ++mp;
+      while (*mp >= 'a' && *mp <= 'z')
+        scMode.push_back(*mp++);
+    }
+    // Set both members directly from the sidecar. strdup UNCONDITIONALLY: do NOT
+    // read the prior force_mode_cfg with strcmp (avoid any deref of a pointer
+    // whose lifetime this code does not own); the tiny per-reload leak of a 1-6
+    // byte string is negligible. "night"/"day" => forced; anything else (auto /
+    // missing / unreadable / garbage) => auto, the safe default.
+    if (scMode == "night") {
+      daynight.enabled = false;
+      daynight.force_mode_cfg = strdup("night");
+    } else if (scMode == "day") {
+      daynight.enabled = false;
+      daynight.force_mode_cfg = strdup("day");
+    } else {
+      daynight.enabled = true;
+      daynight.force_mode_cfg = strdup("");
+    }
+  }
+
   if (!daynight.loglevel || daynight.loglevel[0] == '\0') {
     daynight.loglevel = (general.loglevel && general.loglevel[0] != '\0')
                             ? general.loglevel
